{% extends "core/public_base.htmx.j2" %}
{% load static %}
{% load django_vite %}
{% block title %}Security Advisories · {{ workspace.name }}{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}
    Security advisories published by {{ workspace.name }}: affected products, versions, severity and remediation status.
{% endblock %}
{% block og_title %}{{ workspace.name }} Security Advisories{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
    <h1 class="tc-page-title">{{ workspace.name }} Security Advisories</h1>
    {% comment %}
    The open/closed state of the mobile filter panel. It lives out here, in the
    page shell HTMX never swaps, and the toggle inside the panel is a <label>
    pointing at it — a label binds to its checkbox at click time, so a freshly
    swapped-in one still works. That keeps the panel's state entirely out of the
    swapped DOM, and out of JavaScript: no store to persist, nothing to
    re-initialise after a swap, and it still opens with scripting disabled.
    {% endcomment %}
    <input type="checkbox"
           id="tcFiltersOpen"
           class="tc-filters-state"
           aria-label="Show filters">
    {% include "core/components/trust_center/advisories_browse.html.j2" %}
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
    {% vite_asset 'sbomify/apps/core/js/main.ts' %}
{% endblock %}
